#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:101 4a8eccb592804c4c87d0970e4f309638
msgid ""
"Python 3.11 is the oldest currently maintained Python version receiving "
"security updates (through October 2027)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:104 6b014bb64646410281d8df5ba32c2e13
msgid ""
"Supporting Python < 3.10 would require downgrading data models, "
"discarding `slots=True`, introducing verbose `typing.Union` constructs, "
"and freezing dependencies to outdated versions with unpatched "
"vulnerabilities. Python 3.10 itself no longer receives security fixes, "
"and dependencies have started shipping security fixes only for Python "
"3.11+ (for example, `filelock` 4.2.1). Supporting it would also keep the "
"`tomli` and `typing_extensions.Self` shims alive. Therefore, `requires-"
"python = \">=3.11\"` is technically sound and necessary."
msgstr ""

