#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:143 b253db77bcf248008937c6f6b1185044
msgid "4. Multi-Platform CI Matrix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:145 5b598e0c9ae34396bf7177df9738519a
msgid ""
"Automated verification runs across all certified runtimes and operating "
"systems. Every advertised version (3.11–3.15) is a gating job on all "
"three operating systems. The next feature release runs as an experimental"
" `3.16-dev` job: it may use pre-release interpreters, never blocks a "
"merge, skips the Codecov upload, and is not advertised with a Trove "
"classifier. Until a 3.16 build is available on the runners, the job "
"reports a warning and skips the test run instead of falling back to the "
"runner's default Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:164 fe6ab4079e63491e90c1425578208f33
msgid "5. Python Version Support Lifecycle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:166 bd53e27354d74c39869e8101c0bf53ef
msgid ""
"`findfmt` supports every CPython feature release from the oldest version "
"still receiving security fixes to the newest stable release, and tests "
"the next release early without advertising it. Each change below is "
"guarded by `tests/unit/test_python_support_policy.py`, so a partial "
"update fails CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:170 9f595f48a60644e6b34e40ce16e03623
msgid "5.1. When the Oldest Version Reaches End of Life"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:172 e1c0a0e28cdd4c71b96eef49d0a23aea
msgid ""
"Raise `requires-python` in `pyproject.toml`, remove the old Trove "
"classifier, and raise ruff's `target-version`. Re-lock with `uv lock` and"
" regenerate `.clusterfuzzlite/requirements.txt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:174 7cc2d563b0dc417ebfc45d316112e49b
msgid ""
"Remove the version from the `test-matrix` in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, "
"and remove compatibility code that only the old version needed "
"(`sys.version_info` guards and fallback imports). In the `packaging-"
"smoke-test` job, raise the minimum `python-version` and the Python that "
"`pip` must refuse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:178 35fec233b402417f857d3fc5c993e788
msgid ""
"**Just before merging**, remove the three `Test (<os> - Python <old>)` "
"required status checks from branch protection on `main`. Otherwise the "
"pull request waits for checks that no longer run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:180 db5c9eeb8c7f43fe83c11282f6a848a9
msgid ""
"Update the supported range in this guide, `docs/source/quality/index.md`,"
" `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `SECURITY.md`, and `assets/social-preview.svg` (then "
"regenerate the PNG), regenerate the documentation catalogs (`make -C docs"
" intl-update`), and record the change as breaking in the changelog. "
"Python 3.10 was dropped this way in #441."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:185 63448808d4e0419e9b29ba6014d5382f
msgid "5.2. When a New Version Is Released"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:187 f67656b97dc547588645b0d616519547
msgid ""
"Move the version from the experimental `<version>-dev` matrix entry into "
"the gating `python-version` list, and point the experimental entry at the"
" next feature release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:189 9daa0b96e71848f4bfedbf619773a011
msgid ""
"Add the new Trove classifier and raise `pyproject-fmt --max-supported-"
"python` in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:191 a309c646f2d348ba94b5da4e8e3ddd85
msgid ""
"Move the single-interpreter jobs (quality gate, documentation, and "
"release) and the maximum `python-version` of the packaging smoke test to "
"the new version once the toolchain passes on it. Update the container "
"image when matching `uv` builder and Python runtime images exist for the "
"same Debian release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:195 d23f621154f44f4b821eb84b94f5edb0
msgid ""
"**After the new jobs report green**, add the three `Test (<os> - Python "
"<new>)` checks to the required status checks on `main`. Never require the"
" experimental job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:197 1709796602f14ec6a7e6e1d0cd2a7757
msgid ""
"Update the docs as in step 4 of §5.1. Python 3.15 was added this way in "
"#335 and #440."
msgstr ""
